{"delta":"{"confidence":0.8,"dependencies":[],"files":[{"change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "// ErrNotFound is returned when a session id is unknown or has expired.\nvar ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"session not found\")\n\n// ErrInvalidID is returned when a session id fails boundary validation.\nvar ErrInvalidID = errors.New(\"invalid session id\")\n\n// ValidID reports whether id is an acceptable session id: non-empty,\n// at most 128 characters, and free of whitespace or control characters.\nfunc ValidID(id string) bool {\n\tif id == \"\" || len(id) > 128 {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfor _, r := range id {\n\t\tif r == ' ' || r == '\\t' || r == '\\n' || r == '\\r' || r < 0x20 || r == 0x7f {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}", "old": "// ErrNotFound is returned when a session id is unknown or has expired.\nvar ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"session not found\")"}, {"new": "func (s *Store) Get(id string) (Session, error) {\n\tif !ValidID(id) {\n\t\treturn Session{}, ErrInvalidID\n\t}\n\ts.mu.Lock()", "old": "func (s *Store) Get(id string) (Session, error) {\n\ts.mu.Lock()"}], "path": "session.go"}, {"change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "store := NewStore(30 * time.Minute)\n\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/session\", sessionHandler(store))\n\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/admin/session\", adminSessionHandler(store))", "old": "store := NewStore(30 * time.Minute)\n\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/session\", sessionHandler(store))"}, {"new": "\t\tcase http.MethodGet:\n\t\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\twriteLookupError(w, err)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\twriteJSON(w, session)", "old": "\t\tcase http.MethodGet:\n\t\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\twriteJSON(w, session)"}, {"new": "// adminSessionHandler is a read-only admin lookup that answers the same\n// JSON as GET /session for a given id.\nfunc adminSessionHandler(store *Store) http.HandlerFunc {\n\treturn func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\tif r.Method != http.MethodGet {\n\t\t\thttp.Error(w, \"method not allowed\", http.StatusMethodNotAllowed)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\twriteLookupError(w, err)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\twriteJSON(w, session)\n\t}\n}\n\n// writeLookupError maps store errors to status codes, reusing the\n// ErrInvalidID path rather than re-implementing validation.\nfunc writeLookupError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {\n\tswitch {\n\tcase errors.Is(err, ErrInvalidID):\n\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusBadRequest)\n\tdefault:\n\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n\t}\n}\n\n// healthHandler reports how many sessions are currently held.", "old": "// healthHandler reports how many sessions are currently held."}, {"new": "import (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"time\"\n)", "old": "import (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"time\"\n)"}], "path": "main.go"}],"intent":"Add a ValidID validation convention plus ErrInvalidID at the store level (enforced in Store.Get), and expose GET /admin/session reusing that same store error path, answering 400 for invalid ids and 404 for unknown/expired ones; GET /session now maps errors through the same shared mapping.","known_limitations":["The exact validation convention for session ids was truncated in the input; implemented a reasonable rule (non-empty, <=128 chars, no whitespace/control characters). Adjust if the repo convention differs.", "No admin handler tests were authored here; the test_runner stage should cover 400/404 behavior for /admin/session and /session.", "Store.Create and Delete still accept unvalidated ids; only the lookup path enforces validation per the intent."],"language":"go"}","id":"call_03d29a8da1d54dcba1a38518","runId":"run_20260911172220_c54ae2","schemaVersion":2,"type":"tool_call_delta"}
