{"delta":"{"confidence": 0.75, "dependencies": [], "files": [{"change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "// ErrNotFound is returned when a session id is unknown or has expired.\nvar ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"session not found\")\n\n// ErrInvalidID is returned when a session id fails boundary validation.\nvar ErrInvalidID = errors.New(\"invalid session id\")\n\n// ValidID reports whether a session id passes validation.\nfunc ValidID(id string) bool {\n\treturn id != \"\"\n}", "old": "// ErrNotFound is returned when a session id is unknown or has expired.\nvar ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"session not found\")"}, {"new": "func (s *Store) Get(id string) (Session, error) {\n\tif !ValidID(id) {\n\t\treturn Session{}, ErrInvalidID\n\t}\n\ts.mu.Lock()", "old": "func (s *Store) Get(id string) (Session, error) {\n\ts.mu.Lock()"}], "path": ""}, {"change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "\tcase http.MethodGet:\n\t\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\twriteJSON(w, session)\n\t\tdefault:", "old": "\tcase http.MethodGet:\n\t\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\twriteJSON(w, session)\n\t\tdefault:"}, {"new": "// adminSessionHandler is a read-only lookup that answers the same JSON as\n// GET /session, reusing the store's validation rule at its boundary.\nfunc adminSessionHandler(store *Store) http.HandlerFunc {\n\treturn func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\tif r.Method != http.MethodGet {\n\t\t\thttp.Error(w, \"method not allowed\", http.StatusMethodNotAllowed)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\tswitch {\n\t\tcase errors.Is(err, ErrInvalidID):\n\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusBadRequest)\n\t\tcase err != nil:\n\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\twriteJSON(w, session)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// healthHandler reports how many sessions are currently held.", "old": "// healthHandler reports how many sessions are currently held."}, {"new": "import (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"time\"\n)", "old": "import (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"time\"\n)"}, {"new": "\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/session\", sessionHandler(store))\n\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/admin/session\", adminSessionHandler(store))", "old": "\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/session\", sessionHandler(store))"}], "path": "main.go"}, {"change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tstatus := http.StatusNotFound\n\t\t\t\tif errors.Is(err, ErrInvalidID) {\n\t\t\t\t\tstatus = http.StatusBadRequest\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), status)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}", "old": "\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}"}], "path": "main.go"}], "intent": "Add a read-only GET /admin/session handler that reuses the store's id validation: Store.Get returns a new ErrInvalidID for ids failing the validation rule, and the admin handler maps it to 400 while not-found maps to 404 and valid ids answer the same session JSON as GET /session.", "known_limitations": ["The full validation convention from the (unseen) session tests was truncated in the input; ValidID is implemented as the conservative non-empty rule. If the convention requires more (e.g. charset limits), only ValidID needs updating.", "GET /session behavior for invalid ids changes from 404 to 400 since it shares Store.Get; existing session_test.go expectations were not available to confirm this is acceptable.", "No tests were generated in this stage; test coverage is left to the pipeline's test stages."], "language": "go", "memory_disposition": []}","id":"call_cdb32f08164f443498a9a376","runId":"run_20260911172220_c54ae2","schemaVersion":2,"type":"tool_call_delta"}
