{"delta":"{"confidence": 0.82, "dependencies": [], "files": [{"change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "import (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n)", "old": "import (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n)"}, {"new": "// ErrNotFound is returned when a session id is unknown or has expired.\nvar ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"session not found\")\n\n// ErrInvalidID is returned when a session id fails boundary validation.\nvar ErrInvalidID = errors.New(\"invalid session id\")\n\n// validateID is the single id-validation convention shared by every store path:\n// an id must be non-empty, free of whitespace, and at most 64 characters.\nfunc validateID(id string) error {\n\tif id == \"\" || len(id) > 64 || strings.ContainsAny(id, \" \\t\\r\\n\") {\n\t\treturn ErrInvalidID\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}", "old": "// ErrNotFound is returned when a session id is unknown or has expired.\nvar ErrNotFound = errors.New(\"session not found\")"}, {"new": "func (s *Store) Get(id string) (Session, error) {\n\tif err := validateID(id); err != nil {\n\t\treturn Session{}, err\n\t}\n\ts.mu.Lock()", "old": "func (s *Store) Get(id string) (Session, error) {\n\ts.mu.Lock()"}, {"new": "// Lookup returns a live session without refreshing its last-seen time.\n// It applies the same validation and expiry rules as Get.\nfunc (s *Store) Lookup(id string) (Session, error) {\n\tif err := validateID(id); err != nil {\n\t\treturn Session{}, err\n\t}\n\ts.mu.RLock()\n\tdefer s.mu.RUnlock()\n\tsession, ok := s.sessions[id]\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn Session{}, ErrNotFound\n\t}\n\tif s.now().Sub(session.LastSeen) > s.ttl {\n\t\treturn Session{}, ErrNotFound\n\t}\n\treturn session, nil\n}\n\n// Delete removes a session.", "old": "// Delete removes a session."}], "path": ""}, {"base_ref": "main.go", "change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "import (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"time\"\n)", "old": "import (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"time\"\n)"}, {"new": "\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/session\", sessionHandler(store))\n\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/admin/session\", adminSessionHandler(store))\n\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/healthz\", healthHandler(store))", "old": "\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/session\", sessionHandler(store))\n\thttp.HandleFunc(\"/healthz\", healthHandler(store))"}, {"new": "\t\tcase http.MethodGet:\n\t\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\twriteGetError(w, err)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\twriteJSON(w, session)", "old": "\t\tcase http.MethodGet:\n\t\t\tsession, err := store.Get(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\twriteJSON(w, session)"}, {"new": "// adminSessionHandler is a read-only admin lookup answering the same JSON\n// as GET /session, reusing the store's ErrInvalidID validation path.\nfunc adminSessionHandler(store *Store) http.HandlerFunc {\n\treturn func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\tif r.Method != http.MethodGet {\n\t\t\thttp.Error(w, \"method not allowed\", http.StatusMethodNotAllowed)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tsession, err := store.Lookup(r.URL.Query().Get(\"id\"))\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\twriteGetError(w, err)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\twriteJSON(w, session)\n\t}\n}\n\n// writeGetError maps store errors to status codes: invalid ids are a 400,\n// everything else a 404.\nfunc writeGetError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {\n\tif errors.Is(err, ErrInvalidID) {\n\t\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusBadRequest)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\thttp.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusNotFound)\n}\n\n// healthHandler reports how many sessions are currently held.", "old": "// healthHandler reports how many sessions are currently held."}], "path": ""}, {"change_type": "modify", "edits": [{"new": "// Store keeps sessions in memory. Everything is lost when the process exits.", "old": "// Store keeps sessions in memory. Everything is lost when the process exits."}], "path": ""}, {"path": "main.go", "change_type": "modify", "base_ref": "main.go", "edits": []}], "intent": "Add a single validateID convention in session.go returning ErrInvalidID, have Store.Get and a new read-only Store.Lookup reuse it, and register GET /admin/session that answers the same JSON as GET /session with invalid ids mapped to 400.", "known_limitations": ["The exact 'validation convention from the session id' was not visible in provided context (session_test.go was not delivered); implemented the conventional rule (non-empty, no whitespace, max 64 chars) as validateID in session.go so it is shared by both paths.", "The previous run failed before producing output, so there is no prior /admin/session code to modify; these changes are written against the delivered main.go and session.go.", "Static analysis and test results not yet seen; test_runner/static_analyzer should verify ErrInvalidID mapping to 400 and Lookup not refreshing LastSeen."], "language": "go", "memory_disposition": []}","id":"call_ab80d81b66a646f581113b37","runId":"run_20260911172220_c54ae2","schemaVersion":2,"type":"tool_call_delta"}
